<p>San Diego's sunshine is a selling point for tourists and a cost for everyone who lives here: rent is among the highest in the country, and plenty of locals need extra income just to stay near the coast. The good news is that the best side hustles in San Diego plug directly into what makes the city unique — a steady flood of visitors, one of the largest military populations in the country, a biotech cluster on Torrey Pines Mesa and miles of beaches, bays and marinas that need constant upkeep.</p>
<p>Below are 16 side gigs in San Diego with typical pay, startup costs and the neighborhoods where each works best, followed by a quick start plan and the city tax rules most guides skip.</p>

