<h2 id="san-diego-economy">What drives side gigs in San Diego</h2>
<p>Four forces shape demand here, and the best side hustlers pick a gig that rides at least one of them:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Tourism and conventions.</strong> Comic-Con takes over the Convention Center and the Gaslamp every July, the San Diego County Fair and the summer racing season fill Del Mar, and the Zoo, Balboa Park, SeaWorld and the beaches stay busy year-round.</li>
  <li><strong>The military.</strong> Naval Base San Diego, Naval Air Station North Island in Coronado, MCAS Miramar and Camp Pendleton up the coast mean constant moves, deployments and families who need trustworthy help.</li>
  <li><strong>Biotech, tech and universities.</strong> Sorrento Valley and Torrey Pines are packed with life sciences companies, and UC San Diego, San Diego State and USD bring students who need tutoring and parents who pay for it.</li>
  <li><strong>The ocean.</strong> Salt air, sand and thousands of boats in Mission Bay, Shelter Island and Harbor Island create upkeep work you will not find inland.</li>
</ul>

