    <ul class="meta"><li><b>Pay:</b> Typically $30–$45/hr, or 15–25% as co-host</li><li><b>Startup:</b> $75–$150 in supplies</li><li><b>Best for:</b> Fast, detail-oriented workers</li></ul>
  </div>
  <div class="hustle-card">
    <h3 id="rideshare">2. Rideshare around the airport and events</h3>
    <p>San Diego International sits minutes from Downtown, so airport runs are short but frequent. The money windows are Padres games at Petco Park, Comic-Con week, weekend nights in the Gaslamp and North Park, and San Diego FC and Aztecs games at Snapdragon Stadium. See our <a href="/lyft-uber/">Lyft and Uber guide</a> before you sign up.</p>
    <ul class="meta"><li><b>Pay:</b> Typically $18–$30/hr before costs</li><li><b>Startup:</b> Eligible car, insurance</li><li><b>Best for:</b> Event-weekend drivers</li></ul>
  </div>
  <div class="hustle-card">
    <h3 id="surf-fitness">3. Surf lessons and beach fitness</h3>
    <p>Visitors want a first surf lesson and locals want sunrise boot camps. Certified instructors with CPR training and liability insurance can teach private lessons or small groups. San Diego regulates commercial activity on public beaches and parks, so check the city's permit rules before you set up a regular spot.</p>
    <ul class="meta"><li><b>Pay:</b> Typically $60–$120 per private lesson</li><li><b>Startup:</b> Boards, insurance, certification</li><li><b>Best for:</b> Experienced surfers, trainers</li></ul>
